1
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:56,000
There's magic in believing!

2
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:46,000
The Last Unicorn is a fantasy, animation, family
film directed by Arthur Rankin, Jr..

3
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:36,000
A unicorn learns from a riddle-speaking butterfly that she is supposedly the last of her
kind, all the others having been herded away by the monstrous Red Bull.

4
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:26,000
The unicorn sets out to discover the truth behind the butterfly's words.

5
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:16,000
She is eventually joined on her quest by Schmendrick, a second-rate magician, and Molly
Grue, a middle-aged woman who dreamed all her life of seeing a unicorn.

6
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:06,000
Their journey leads them far from home, all the
way to the castle of King Haggard.

7
00:26:50,000 --> 00:26:56,000
Unicorn / Amalthea (voice), played by Mia Farrow.

8
00:30:40,000 --> 00:30:46,000
Schmendrick (voice), played by Alan Arkin.

9
00:34:30,000 --> 00:34:36,000
Molly Grue (voice), played by Tammy Grimes.

10
00:38:20,000 --> 00:38:26,000
Prince Lir (voice), played by Jeff Bridges.

11
00:42:10,000 --> 00:42:16,000
King Haggard (voice), played by Christopher Lee.

12
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:06,000
Mommy Fortuna (voice), played by Angela Lansbury.

13
00:49:50,000 --> 00:49:56,000
The Last Unicorn is a 1982 animated fantasy film
directed and produced by Arthur Rankin Jr.

14
00:53:40,000 --> 00:53:46,000
and Jules Bass, from a script by Peter S.

15
00:57:30,000 --> 00:57:36,000
Beagle adapted from his 1968 novel of the same title.

16
01:01:20,000 --> 01:01:26,000
The plot concerns a unicorn who, upon learning that she is the last of her species on
Earth, goes on a quest to find out what has happened to others of her kind.

17
01:05:10,000 --> 01:05:16,000
It was produced by Rankin/Bass Productions for ITC
Entertainment and animated by Topcraft.

18
01:09:00,000 --> 01:09:06,000
Voice performers include Alan Arkin, Jeff Bridges, Mia
Farrow, Angela Lansbury, and Christopher Lee.

19
01:12:50,000 --> 01:12:56,000
The soundtrack was composed and arranged by Jimmy Webb, and songs were performed by the group America
and the London Symphony Orchestra, with additional vocals provided by Lucy Mitchell.

20
01:16:40,000 --> 01:16:46,000
Although critical reviews were generally positive, the film was a
commercial failure, grossing $6.5 million in the United States.

21
01:20:30,000 --> 01:20:36,000
It has since maintained a cult following.

22
01:24:20,000 --> 01:24:26,000
In 2003, the Online Film Critics Society ranked the film as
the 96th greatest animated film of all time.

23
01:28:10,000 --> 01:28:16,000
The film explores themes of love of one's life, magic,
magic show, prince, sorcerer's apprentice.
